# ---------- default deny ----------
# Blanket-ignore first, then re-include the tracked source surface below.
#
# With only `*`, every NEW file is invisible to `git status` and is skipped by
# `git add -A`, so a commit silently omits work. Five files in the theme and
# accessibility pass needed `git add -f` before this was written, and nothing in
# the output distinguished "already tracked" from "about to be lost".
#
# This is default-deny plus an explicit allowlist. Because a .gitignore never
# affects an already-tracked file, the re-inclusions below cannot untrack
# anything: the worst case is a gap in the list, which shows up as a new file
# staying ignored, not as a deletion.
#
# Git applies the LAST matching pattern, so the order in this file matters:
#   1. `*`                    — deny everything
#   2. the re-inclusions      — un-ignore the source surface
#   3. the junk rules at the end — win over the re-inclusions
*

# ---------- re-include the tracked source surface ----------
#
# Directories. Each one needs BOTH forms, and this is the part that is easy to
# get wrong: `!dir/**` alone has no effect, because git refuses to descend into a
# directory it considers excluded, so the contents are never examined and never
# match. `!dir/` un-ignores the directory itself, which is what lets git descend;
# `!dir/**` then un-ignores what is inside it.
!css/
!css/**
!docs/
!docs/**
!fontawesome/
!fontawesome/**
!images/
!images/**
!js/
!js/**
!.opencode/
!.opencode/**
!portfolio/
!portfolio/**
!scripts/
!scripts/**
!testenv/
!testenv/**
!tests/
!tests/**

# Root-level files, matched by extension. A pattern with no slash matches at any
# depth, so these also cover nested files of the same type.
!*.cjs
!*.html
!*.json
!*.md
!*.sh
!*.txt
!*.xml
!.gitignore

# ---------- artifacts: these come last so they win ----------
# Test dependencies and generated reports. These sit after `!testenv/**` on
# purpose — without that ordering the re-inclusion would expose node_modules.
testenv/*/node_modules/
testenv/*/test-results/
testenv/*/playwright-report/
testenv/browsers/

# Session scratch space.
.tmp/

# Local planning files.
PLANNING.md
TASKS.md

# Editor and OS droppings, including inside re-included directories.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.Zone.Identifier
